.TH ONEDRIVE-CPP 1 "October 2026" "onedrive-cpp @PROJECT_VERSION@" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
onedrive-cpp \- modern C++ OneDrive synchronization client
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B onedrive-cpp
.RI [ options ]
.I command
.PP
.B onedrive-cpp auth
.RI [ options ]
.PP
.B onedrive-cpp logout
.RI [ options ]
.PP
.B onedrive-cpp reset-state
.RI [ options ]
.PP
.B onedrive-cpp sync
.RI [ options ]
.PP
.B onedrive-cpp monitor
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B onedrive-cpp
is an independent, open-source client intended to authenticate with Microsoft
and synchronize files through Microsoft Graph and OneDrive.
.PP
The current release includes configuration loading, device-code
authentication, authenticated Microsoft Graph delta queries, local state and
delta-link storage, safe one-way downloads, dry-run support, logging,
monitoring scaffolding, and packaging integration. Uploads and local removal
of remotely deleted files are not implemented.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B auth
Authorize the application with Microsoft using the OAuth 2.0 device-code flow.
On success, save the refresh token in the configured state directory.
.TP
.B logout
Remove the locally stored refresh token. This does not revoke consent on the
Microsoft account; revoke the application separately in Microsoft account
settings when required.
.TP
.B reset-state
Reset the saved delta link for the configured drive. This preserves
authentication, configuration, local files, item snapshots, pending-download
recovery records, blocked-item records, and state for other drives. The next
.B sync
recovers pending downloads and performs a full initial delta query for the
configured drive. The complete remote inventory replaces old item metadata;
items that still conflict are recorded as blocked.
.PP
With
.BR \-\-clear\-all ,
remove item snapshots, the delta link, pending-download recovery records, and
blocked items for the configured drive. The command requires the configured
drive ID as interactive confirmation. Local files and other drives remain
untouched, but the next sync may report local modification conflicts. For automation,
.B \-\-yes
explicitly confirms
.BR \-\-clear\-all ;
it is rejected without that option.
.TP
.B sync
Refresh the OAuth access token and retrieve recursive drive changes using the
Microsoft Graph delta API. Successful non-dry-run queries atomically persist
remote metadata and the final delta link after creating directories and safely
downloading added or changed files. Downloads use same-directory temporary
files, size validation, flushing, and atomic replacement. Existing local files
that cannot be proven unchanged are persisted as blocked items instead of being
overwritten. Invalid names, local path conflicts, files marked with the
Microsoft Graph malware facet, and descendants of blocked directories are also
isolated while independent files continue. Malware-marked files are not
downloaded or allowed to replace local data. A partial completion exits with
status 2, and blocked items are retried on later syncs. Installed files use the
authoritative fileSystemInfo.lastModifiedDateTime value; files without a valid
value are rejected before download. Permissions are derived from mode 0666 and
the process umask.
SQLite pending-download records and SHA-256 content fingerprints provide
crash recovery independently of target-file-system extended attributes.
Downloads starting at byte zero calculate SHA-256 and QuickXorHash while data
is written and reuse the streamed SHA-256 recovery fingerprint. Resumed or
non-contiguous transfers fall back to hashing the completed file.
Range chunks are accepted only when HTTP status, Content-Range, total size, and
received byte count exactly match the request; rejected chunks are rolled back
to the preceding durable offset.
Microsoft Graph HTTP 408, 429, 502, 503, and 504 responses are retried using
.B Retry-After
or bounded exponential backoff, with a finite retry limit. A pre-authenticated
download URL that returns HTTP 401 or 403 is refreshed through Graph once.
Remote deletion records do not remove local files. Use
.B \-\-dry\-run
to display the download plan without creating files or updating synchronization
state.
.TP
.B monitor
Start the long-running filesystem monitor.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Display help for the application or selected subcommand and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Display the application version and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-clear\-all
With
.BR reset-state ,
remove all saved synchronization state for the configured drive after
confirmation.
.TP
.B \-\-yes
Confirm
.B reset-state \-\-clear\-all
without an interactive prompt. This option is invalid without
.BR \-\-clear\-all .
.TP
.BI \-\-config " PATH"
Read application configuration from
.IR PATH .
The default is
.I ~/.config/onedrive-cpp/config.toml
when
.B HOME
is available, otherwise
.IR /etc/onedrive-cpp/onedrive-cpp.toml .
.TP
.BI \-\-log\-level " LEVEL"
Set the minimum log level. Supported values are
.BR trace ,
.BR debug ,
.BR info ,
.BR warn ,
.BR error ,
.BR critical ,
and
.BR off .
The default is
.BR info .
.TP
.BI \-\-log\-file " PATH"
Also write logs to
.IR PATH .
The file rotates at 5 MiB and retains three older files. Diagnostics continue
to be written to standard error.
.TP
.BI \-\-color " MODE"
Control ANSI styling. Supported modes are
.BR auto ,
.BR always ,
and
.BR never .
The default
.B auto
enables styling only when standard output is a terminal and
.B NO_COLOR
is not set.
.TP
.BI \-\-output " FORMAT"
Select
.B text
or
.B json
command output. JSON output uses one compact object per line, never contains
ANSI sequences, and requires
.B \-\-yes
for destructive operations that would otherwise prompt interactively.
.TP
.B \-\-quiet
Suppress informational and success command output while retaining warnings
and errors. Diagnostic logging remains controlled separately by
.BR \-\-log\-level .
.TP
.B \-\-dry\-run
For the
.B sync
command, display the effective synchronization inputs without modifying
remote files.
.SH CONFIGURATION
The configuration file uses TOML and must declare
.BR "config_version = 1" .
Unknown keys, invalid types, and unsupported configuration versions are
rejected.
.PP
Before a command runs, the state directory is restricted to mode 0700 and an
exclusive
.I onedrive-cpp.lock
is held there. Token and SQLite paths must be regular files owned by the
current user; private state files are restricted to mode 0600. Symbolic links
in state paths are rejected.
.PP
For synchronization, the sync and state directories must not overlap, the
filesystem root cannot be used as the sync directory, and symbolic-link path
components are rejected. Normal synchronization verifies create, write,
flush, and removal behavior with a temporary probe. Download capacity retains
a safety reserve of 256 MiB or five percent of planned transfer bytes,
whichever is larger.
.TP
.B sync.directory
Root directory for synchronized data. Actual content is stored under
.IR accounts/<display-name>--<user-id-hash>/drives/<drive-name>--<drive-id-hash>
so multiple Microsoft users and Drives remain isolated. Files from the former
flat layout are not moved automatically.
.TP
.B sync.permissions
Local permission policy for synchronized data.
.B private
creates files as 0600 and secures the synchronization root and new directories
as 0700.
.B umask
uses the process umask and is intended only for explicitly shared directories.
The default is
.BR private .
.TP
.B state.directory
Directory containing the refresh token and SQLite synchronization state.
.TP
.B sync.drive_id
Microsoft Graph drive identifier. The default is
.BR me .
.TP
.B auth.application_id
Microsoft Entra Application (client) ID.
.TP
.B auth.tenant_id
Microsoft identity tenant selector, such as
.BR common ,
.BR consumers ,
or a specific tenant ID. Use
.B common
for an application registered for both organizational and personal accounts.
.TP
.B auth.endpoint
Microsoft identity endpoint. The default is
.IR https://login.microsoftonline.com .
.TP
.B auth.scopes
Array of delegated OAuth scope strings. Personal Microsoft accounts should
start with
.BR [\(dqUser.Read\(dq,\ \(dqFiles.ReadWrite\(dq,\ \(dqoffline_access\(dq] .
The broader
.B Files.ReadWrite.All
and
.B Sites.ReadWrite.All
scopes must be configured explicitly and produce a warning during
authentication.
.TP
.B graph.throttle.maximum_retries
Maximum number of retries for a retryable Microsoft Graph or file-download
response. The default is
.BR 4 .
.TP
.B graph.throttle.initial_delay_seconds
Initial exponential-backoff delay when a retryable response has no valid numeric
.B Retry-After
header. The default is
.BR 1 .
.TP
.B graph.throttle.maximum_delay_seconds
Maximum accepted or calculated Graph throttling delay. The default is
.B 300
seconds. This value must be greater than or equal to
.BR graph.throttle.initial_delay_seconds .
.TP
.B sync.download_chunk_threshold_bytes
Files larger than this value use sequential HTTP Range requests with this
maximum chunk size. The default is
.B 8388608
bytes and the value must be greater than zero.
.TP
.B sync.download_checkpoint_interval_bytes
Flush and record resumable download progress after this many newly downloaded
bytes. The default is
.B 1048576
bytes and the value must be greater than zero. Smaller values reduce repeated
downloads after interruption but increase synchronization and database
overhead.
.TP
.B sync.download_connect_timeout_seconds
Connection timeout for each file download request. The default is
.B 30
seconds and the value must be greater than zero.
.TP
.B sync.download_operation_timeout_seconds
Maximum duration of each file download request. The default is
.B 3600
seconds and the value must be greater than zero.
.TP
.B sync.download_stall_timeout_seconds
Abort a download that remains below the configured minimum rate for this many
seconds. The default is
.BR 60 ;
zero disables stall detection.
.TP
.B sync.download_stall_minimum_bytes_per_second
Minimum transfer rate used by stall detection. The default is
.B 1
byte per second and the value must be greater than zero.
.TP
.B sync.download_maximum_rate_bytes_per_second
Maximum receive rate for each download. The default is
.BR 0 ,
which disables rate limiting.
.TP
.B sync.download_http_version
HTTP version preference for file downloads:
.BR auto ,
.BR 1.1 ,
or
.BR 2 .
The default is
.BR auto .
.TP
.B sync.download_validation
Remote metadata validation policy:
.B strict
requires the downloaded size and any Graph-provided content hash to match;
.B relaxed
accepts SharePoint, AIP, or HEIC content that differs from Graph metadata and
disables resumable and chunked downloads. Relaxed downloads reserve disk space
incrementally from actual transfer progress and abort if that reservation
cannot grow safely. The default is
.BR strict .
Relaxed mode weakens integrity guarantees.
.TP
.B filesystem.metadata
File-system metadata policy:
.B auto
probes user extended attributes and otherwise uses only the SQLite recovery
journal;
.B xattr
requires extended-attribute support; and
.B database
never reads or writes extended attributes. The default is
.BR auto .
.TP
.B sync.dry_run
Boolean value
.B true
or
.BR false .
.SH SHELL COMPLETION
Bash and Zsh completion definitions are installed with the package. They
complete subcommands, command options, enumerated option values, and paths for
file-valued options.
.PP
For an uninstalled development tree, enable Bash completion in the current
shell with:
.PP
.EX
source packaging/completions/onedrive-cpp.bash
.EE
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/onedrive-cpp/config.toml
Default per-user configuration file.
.TP
.I /etc/onedrive-cpp/onedrive-cpp.toml
System-wide example and fallback configuration.
.TP
.I ~/.local/state/onedrive-cpp/refresh_token
Default locally stored OAuth refresh token. The file is created with
owner-only permissions.
.TP
.I ~/.local/state/onedrive-cpp/items.sqlite3
Default SQLite synchronization-state database.
.TP
.I /usr/lib/systemd/user/onedrive-cpp.service
systemd user service installed by the package.
.SH LOGGING
Diagnostics are written to standard error. A systemd user service captures
that stream in the journal. Follow service logs with:
.PP
.RS
.B journalctl \-\-user \-u onedrive-cpp.service \-f
.RE
.PP
OAuth tokens, device codes, authorization headers, and passwords must not be
written to logs. Take care before sharing debug output because local paths and
file metadata may still be sensitive.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B HOME
Used to determine default configuration, state, and synchronization paths.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
The command completed successfully, or help/version information was shown.
.TP
.B 1
A runtime, configuration, authentication, storage, or synchronization error
occurred.
.TP
.B 2
The command line was invalid.
.SH EXAMPLES
Authorize a Microsoft account:
.PP
.RS
.B onedrive-cpp auth \-\-config ~/.config/onedrive-cpp/config.toml
.RE
.PP
Inspect synchronization inputs:
.PP
.RS
.B onedrive-cpp sync \-\-dry\-run \-\-log\-level debug
.RE
.PP
Run the monitor with a rotating log file:
.PP
.RS
.B onedrive-cpp monitor \-\-log\-file ~/.local/state/onedrive-cpp/onedrive-cpp.log
.RE
.SH SECURITY
Protect the state directory and refresh token as account credentials. Do not
publish tokens, device codes, authorization headers, private file names, or
file contents in logs or issue reports.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR journalctl (1),
.BR systemctl (1),
.BR systemd.service (5)
.PP
Project documentation:
.UR https://github.com/cloudfyy/onedrivecpp
.UE
.SH BUGS
Report bugs at:
.UR https://github.com/cloudfyy/onedrivecpp/issues
.UE
.PP
Do not include passwords, OAuth tokens, device codes, or private file contents
in a bug report.
